window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-2b09a0f3c8670621"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"import-from-another-agent\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">从另一个智能体导入</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需完整的文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 后添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>使用导入流程，可以把另一个智能体中的指令、设置、Skills、Plugins、项目和最近工作带入 ChatGPT 桌面应用或 Codex CLI。桌面应用支持从 <strong>Claude Code</strong>、<strong>Claude Cowork</strong> 或 <strong>Cursor</strong> 导入；Codex CLI 支持从 <strong>Claude Code</strong> 或 <strong>Cursor</strong> 导入。</p> <p>桌面应用会直接导入受支持的内容，并让你完成那些仍需授权的已导入 Plugins 或连接的设置。你还可以通过自动更新，让导入的工作与原智能体保持同步。</p> <p>导入不会更改或删除你现有的智能体设置。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：ChatGPT 导入界面，用于选择要从哪些其它 AI 应用导入</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"start-an-import\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">开始导入</h2> <p><a id=\"import-in-the-desktop-app\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_3\">在桌面应用中导入</h3> <ol> <li>在 ChatGPT 桌面应用中打开 <strong>Settings &gt; Import（设置 &gt; 导入）</strong>。如果设置中还没有 <strong>Import（导入）</strong> 这一项，请打开 <strong>General（通用）</strong>，然后找到 <strong>Import other agent setup（导入其它智能体设置）</strong>。</li> <li>选择 <strong>Import（导入）</strong>。</li> <li>选择要从中导入的智能体，然后选择 <strong>Continue（继续）</strong>。</li> <li>在 <strong>Select items to import（选择要导入的内容）</strong> 页面中，选择要带入的内容，然后选择 <strong>Continue（继续）</strong>。</li> <li>导入完成后，打开一个已导入的项目或聊天以继续工作。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"keep-imported-work-in-sync\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_4\">让导入的工作保持同步</h3> <p>在 ChatGPT 桌面应用中打开 <strong>Settings &gt; Import（设置 &gt; 导入）</strong>，然后开启自动更新，使导入的工作与原智能体保持同步。你也可以在同一个设置页面查看导入历史记录。</p> <p><a id=\"import-in-codex-cli\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"codex-cli\">在 Codex CLI 中导入</h3> <ol> <li>启动本地 Codex CLI 会话，然后输入 <code>/import</code>。</li> <li>选择 <strong>Claude Code</strong> 或 <strong>Cursor</strong>。</li> <li>选择受支持的设置、项目文件和最近聊天。</li> <li>检查导入的配置，然后继续工作。</li> </ol> <p>Codex CLI 最多会导入过去 30 天内的 50 个聊天。在任务运行期间、远程会话中，或连接到本地 app-server 守护进程时，<code>/import</code> 命令不可用。请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?sectionMissing=cli-import-claude-code-or-cursor-setup-with-import\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">CLI 斜杠命令（官网章节，需联网）</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3\">本地页面（未识别该章节）</a>。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：ChatGPT 导入界面，用于选择要导入的设置、项目和最近聊天</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"how-importing-works\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">导入的工作方式</h2> <p>导入流程会同时检查你的用户级设置和现有项目。用户级设置来自电脑上的文件，项目级设置则来自你选择的代码仓库和文件夹。</p> <p>导入时，ChatGPT 会：</p> <ol> <li>检测受支持的设置和最近工作。</li> <li>导入你选择的内容。</li> <li>保持你现有的智能体设置不变。</li> <li>检查导入的 Plugins 或连接是否仍需设置。</li> <li>在你需要完成设置时显示状态卡片。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"what-chatgpt-can-import\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"chatgpt\">ChatGPT 可以导入哪些内容</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>导入内容</th> <th>目标位置</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>指令文件</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-94f17e3de1ca7cb3\"><code>AGENTS.md</code></a></td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>settings.json</code></td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76\"><code>config.toml</code></a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>技能（Skills）</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">技能</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>插件（Plugins）</td> <td>插件</td> </tr> <tr> <td>现有项目文件夹</td> <td>继续使用相同文件夹的项目</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Claude Code 项目记忆</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-7ea5a1f5cc6a25bc\">记忆</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>最近 30 天内的聊天</td> <td>ChatGPT 聊天</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MCP 服务器配置</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\">Codex MCP 配置</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>钩子（Hooks）</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-0aecdb1ef0cec0a4\">Codex 钩子</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>斜杠命令</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">技能</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>子代理（Subagents）</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-731168d993ec5d2b\">Codex 子代理</a></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"finish-setup-after-importing\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">导入后完成设置</h2> <p>导入完成后，应用会在左下角显示一张状态卡片。如果某个已导入的 Plugin 或连接仍需设置，该卡片会明确指出。</p> <p>当应用标出需要你处理的项目时，选择 <strong>Finish（完成）</strong>，然后按照提示完成设置。</p> <p><a id=\"what-to-review-after-importing\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">导入后应检查什么</h2> <p>在依赖已导入的设置之前，请先检查它们，尤其注意：</p> <ul> <li>已导入 Skills 和智能体中的工具限制或权限。</li> <li>使用自定义身份验证、请求头、环境变量或传输方式的 MCP server 设置。你可能需要重新登录。</li> <li>导入后行为可能不同的 Hooks。</li> <li>仍需手动完成设置的 Plugins、marketplaces 或其它配置。</li> <li>依赖参数、shell 插值或文件路径占位符的提示词模板或命令式提示词。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"after-you-import\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">导入之后</h2> <p>导入完成后，打开一个已导入的项目并继续工作。请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-d6b5aa6a43ce8c0f\">使用 ChatGPT</a>，了解如何开始下一个任务。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"import-from-another-agent\">Import from another agent</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Use the import flow to bring instructions, settings, skills, plugins, projects, and recent work from another agent into the ChatGPT desktop app or Codex CLI. The desktop app can import from <strong>Claude Code</strong>, <strong>Claude Cowork</strong>, or <strong>Cursor</strong>. Codex CLI can import from <strong>Claude Code</strong> or <strong>Cursor</strong>.</p> <p>The desktop app imports supported items directly and lets you finish setup for imported plugins or connections that need authorization. You can also keep imported work in sync with automatic updates.</p> <p>Importing doesn't change or delete your existing agent setup.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: ChatGPT import screen for choosing other AI apps to import from.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"start-an-import\">Start an import</h2> <h3 id=\"import-in-the-desktop-app\">Import in the desktop app</h3> <ol> <li>In the ChatGPT desktop app, open <strong>Settings &gt; Import</strong>. If <strong>Import</strong> isn't available as a settings section yet, open <strong>General</strong> and find <strong>Import other agent setup</strong>.</li> <li>Select <strong>Import</strong>.</li> <li>Choose the agents you want to import from, then select <strong>Continue</strong>.</li> <li>On <strong>Select items to import</strong>, choose what to bring over, then select <strong>Continue</strong>.</li> <li>After the import finishes, open an imported project or chat to continue working.</li> </ol> <h3 id=\"keep-imported-work-in-sync\">Keep imported work in sync</h3> <p>In the ChatGPT desktop app, open <strong>Settings &gt; Import</strong> and turn on automatic updates to keep imported work in sync with the original agent. You can also review your import history from the same settings section.</p> <h3 id=\"import-in-codex-cli\">Import in Codex CLI</h3> <ol> <li>Start a local Codex CLI session and type <code>/import</code>.</li> <li>Choose <strong>Claude Code</strong> or <strong>Cursor</strong>.</li> <li>Select the supported setup, project files, and recent chats you want to import.</li> <li>Review the imported configuration and continue working in Codex.</li> </ol> <p>Codex CLI imports up to 50 chats from the last 30 days. The <code>/import</code> command isn't available during a running task, in a remote session, or while connected to a local app-server daemon. See <a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?sectionMissing=cli-import-claude-code-or-cursor-setup-with-import\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">CLI slash commands (official section, online)</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3\">Local page (section not recognized)</a>.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: ChatGPT import screen for selecting setup, projects, and recent chats to import.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"how-importing-works\">How importing works</h2> <p>The import flow checks both your user-level setup and your existing projects. User-level setup comes from files on your machine. Project-level setup comes from files in the repositories and folders you select.</p> <p>When you import, ChatGPT:</p> <ol> <li>Detects supported setup and recent work.</li> <li>Imports the items you select.</li> <li>Leaves your existing agent setup unchanged.</li> <li>Checks whether imported plugins or connections still need setup.</li> <li>Shows a status card when you need to finish setup.</li> </ol> <h2 id=\"what-chatgpt-can-import\">What ChatGPT can import</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Imported item</th> <th>Destination</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Instruction files</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-94f17e3de1ca7cb3\"><code>AGENTS.md</code></a></td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>settings.json</code></td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76\"><code>config.toml</code></a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Skills</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">Skills</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Plugins</td> <td>Plugins</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Existing project folders</td> <td>Projects using the same folders</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Project memories from Claude Code</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-7ea5a1f5cc6a25bc\">Memories</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Chats from the last 30 days</td> <td>ChatGPT chats</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MCP server configuration</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\">Codex MCP configuration</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Hooks</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-0aecdb1ef0cec0a4\">Codex hooks</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Slash commands</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">Skills</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Subagents</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-731168d993ec5d2b\">Codex subagents</a></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"finish-setup-after-importing\">Finish setup after importing</h2> <p>When the import completes, the app shows a status card in the lower-left corner. If an imported plugin or connection still needs setup, the card calls it out.</p> <p>When the app flags an item that needs attention, select <strong>Finish</strong> and follow the prompts to complete setup.</p> <h2 id=\"what-to-review-after-importing\">What to review after importing</h2> <p>Review imported setup before you rely on it, especially:</p> <ul> <li>Tool restrictions or permissions in imported skills and agents.</li> <li>MCP server settings that use custom authentication, headers, environment variables, or transports. You may need to sign in again.</li> <li>Hooks whose behavior may differ after import.</li> <li>Plugins, marketplaces, or other setup that needs manual follow-up.</li> <li>Prompt templates or command-style prompts that depend on arguments, shell interpolation, or file-path placeholders.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"after-you-import\">After you import</h2> <p>Once the import finishes, open one of your imported projects and continue from there. See <a href=\"#/article/a-d6b5aa6a43ce8c0f\">Use ChatGPT</a> for guidance on starting your next task.</p>"};
